              "url": "https://lore.kernel.org/all/20261024170415.4121901-1-gourry@gourry.net/",
              "subject": "[PATCH] mm/mempolicy: recompute automatic interleave weights on memory hotplug",
              "date": "2026-10-24T17:04:23Z"
            }
          ],
          "series_items": [],
          "patch_summary": "This patch updates the automatic interleave weights in the Linux kernel's memory policy module to recalculate weights based on node bandwidth when a node gains or loses memory. The previous behavior was to only update weights when a new node reports its bandwidth, leading to incorrect weights being used. The patch introduces a new function `wi_state_refresh` that recalculates the weights from the recorded bandwidth whenever a node gains its first memory or loses its last. This ensures that the weighted interleave mode works correctly even after nodes are added or removed.",
          "analysis_source": "llm-chunked-no-replies",
